# TASK-260715-ypo7yo — handoff evidence, round 3 (verdict-02 rework)

Revision **2026-07-28.r3**. Status: **ready for review**. No portal mutation has
occurred and none is authorized by this handoff.

## 1. What verdict 02 asked for, and what changed

Verdict 02 raised one blocking finding, F1: the accepted project architecture
requires the sandboxed `ReluxProxyMac` host to carry Sparkle's documented Mach
lookup exceptions, the matrix acknowledged them in prose, but never authored the
entitlement — so the r2 exhaustive allowlist (A10b) would have **rejected a
correctly built host**.

| required rework | done | where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Add `com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name` to `macos.host` only, status `required-adjacent`, exact two-value array, `portalCapability` false, owner, `project-architecture` attribution, spec + Sparkle basis | yes | JSON `targets[macos.host].entitlements`; matrix §4.2 **D-6** |
| 2. Validator rule pinning key, target, exact values, attribution, absence elsewhere; negative gates for missing key, wrong value, grant to an unrelated target | yes | `validate_matrix.py` **R25**; `mutate.py` nine `F1-v02` gates |
| 3. Update the Markdown entitlement table, allowlist evidence, handoff evidence, gate log, logbook | yes | §4.2 table + D-6, §9.1 resolved allowlist, §9 assertion table, §9.2, §10, §13; this file; `validate-matrix-03.log`; LOGBOOK |
| 4. Preserve every accepted r2 decision | yes | §3 below |

**Beyond the literal ask, one thing was added.** The same spec clause that
mandates the exception also bans *"unreviewed exception entitlement"*
(`.spec/platform-distribution.md`). Granting the project's first temporary
exception while the contract had no rule about exceptions at all would leave the
matrix weaker than the spec it implements, and would let this defect recur one
key at a time. **Rule X1** (§4.5) adds a reviewed-exception register plus an
explicit banned set for Hardened Runtime relaxations. This is contract
completeness against a literal spec line, not new scope: no board element was
created or changed, and no new capability is granted to any target.

## 2. Independent verification of the finding before accepting it

The finding was re-checked three ways rather than taken on trust.

| source | result |
| --- | --- |
| `.spec/platform-distribution.md:103-105` | Mandates `SUEnableInstallerLauncherService` and the `<host-bundle-id>-spks` / `-spki` Mach lookup exceptions for the sandboxed host. |
