      "summary": "The macos.host entitlement set now carries com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name with Sparkle's $(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)-spks / -spki values, attributed to project-architecture and owned by TASK-260715-uyju7n. Rule X1 adds a reviewed-exception register and an explicit prohibited set for Hardened Runtime relaxations, which is the same spec clause the finding exposed. Assertions A10e, A14 and A15 make all of it machine-checkable, and the r2 assertion set is pinned so it cannot silently shrink again. Every r2 decision — four production identifiers and containment, channel-keyed Network Extension values, identical registered iOS-style App Group literals, Keychain withholding on macos.provider, the legacy no-migration rule, C1 scope, the gap task, and dependencies — is preserved byte-for-byte.",
