description:Decide how one configured SSH profile's private key and optional passphrase reach the macOS packet-tunnel provider, given that the provider is a system extension running as root outside a user context. TASK-260715-ypo7yo established from Apple documentation and DTS guidance that the Data Protection Keychain is available only to code running in a user context and that keychain access groups share items between programs running as the SAME user. The macOS host runs as the logged-in user and the provider runs as root, so the .spec/security-privacy.md design (secrets in the Data Protection Keychain shared through one access group with the packet tunnel extension) cannot work on macOS as written. iOS is unaffected because its appex runs as the same user as its host. This task selects the macOS transport, states its security properties honestly, and defines the entitlement amendment it implies for the identifier matrix.
scope:In scope: the exact question the spec leaves open — by what mechanism does a root-context macOS NEPacketTunnelProvider obtain SSH private-key material and an optional passphrase that the user-context containing app holds, without placing secrets in providerConfiguration, App Group data, logs, or board resources; comparison of at least host-to-provider IPC seeding over NETunnelProviderSession/XPC, the file-based System keychain with an access group, and provider-owned root-context storage; on-demand and boot-time start behaviour when the containing app is not running; secret lifetime and zeroization implications; the resulting amendment (grant or keep prohibited) for keychain-access-groups on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel in the TASK-260715-ypo7yo matrix; the entitlement and portal consequences of the selected option; a physical reachability check on this Apple-silicon Mac where one is needed to settle a documented uncertainty. Out of scope: implementing the vault or the resolver, iOS behaviour, host trust policy, key import or generation, engine selection, UI, and changing the identifier matrix directly — this task produces the amendment, TASK-260715-ypo7yo owns the matrix.
